1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,980
In 1900, Greek sponge divers

2
00:00:02,980 --> 00:00:05,760
pulled a corroded lump of bronze

3
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,920
from an ancient shipwreck.

4
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:11,700
Hidden inside was an analog computer,

5
00:00:11,960 --> 00:00:14,640
so advanced, modern science didn't

6
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:15,440
believe the Greeks

7
00:00:15,420 --> 00:00:17,880
could build it until CT scans

8
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:20,820
proved it in 2006. Found off

9
00:00:20,820 --> 00:00:22,840
the island of Antikythera,

10
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:27,140
this machine was built over 2,100 years ago.

12
00:00:27,140 --> 00:00:30,420
Inside its calcified shell were

13
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,580
more than 30 interlocking bronze

14
00:00:32,580 --> 00:00:35,160
gears with precision triangular

15
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,960
teeth.

16
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,980
A level of engineering history

17
00:00:37,980 --> 00:00:39,780
textbooks claim didn't exist

18
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:43,260
until 14th century European clocks.

19
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:46,420
It wasn't a timepiece. By turning

20
00:00:46,420 --> 00:00:49,340
a hand crank, it calculated solar

21
00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:51,460
eclipses decades in advance,

22
00:00:51,460 --> 00:00:54,240
tracked the Olympic Games, and

23
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:56,640
used an epicyclic pin and slot

24
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:59,660
gear train to replicate the elliptical

25
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,300
speed of the moon.

26
00:01:01,820 --> 00:01:05,800
Over 3,500 ancient Greek characters

27
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:08,320
were engraved across its bronze

28
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:10,540
plates, acting as a complete

29
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:11,680
user manual.

30
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:13,260
It wasn't built by aliens or

31
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:15,960
myth. It was Hellenistic genius,

32
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:18,660
which leaves one haunting question.

33
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:21,640
If humanity built a mechanical

34
00:01:21,640 --> 00:01:25,560
computer in 100 BC, where would

35
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:29,040
our world be today if this technology

36
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:31,780
had never been lost to the sea?
